{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the Mishkan.</b> As He informed him at the outset of the plan of the Mishkan." "<b>Ma'aseh choshev.</b> The Sages said that ma'aseh choshev is two figures, and rokem is one figure, and this is correct. And by way of the plain sense, ma'aseh choshev is neither rokem nor woven, but rather like the way silk garments are made today, for the form that arises in the heart is a reckoning, and its thought, and he depicts it on a board and sets two threads by reckoning to draw from a distance."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:29.262522838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}